ittle bit of have a little bit of a  flexibility with it but it's it's  working and good and we're liking it so  so my first example here is  basically imagine something that you  want to just show up and you in the  online course you don't want to show you  don't want to also show up in just on  the web so this is an example online  course here that I have this text here  that's very small on the screen but it  says this will only be seen within the  course and it's very true so if I go to  that link outside of the course it gives  me this failure messages so sorry you're  not in the course you're not a part of  the course you shouldn't see this thing  and so yeah so we're able to now just  show things as long as you are  authenticated within the course and I do  that just by using this function called  LTI verifier request and so you're  seeing this it's just a cloud object  delayed cloud object where we get this  LTI package and verify that they are  within the course and if they are then  they move on and see this the rest of  the third object so you can imagine in  your course maybe you want to take a  poll of the students there and you don't  want students from outside the course to  interact with this poll so you can set  this up in that same way where you have  LTI there verify request and then you  have some forum function as your cloud  object and you have a data bin you  submit that information to a dative and  make a bar chart and so within the  course have this started somewhere else  within the course you can have this poll  that just shows what's your favorite  flavor of ice cream and you can pick  your favorite flavor submit it and see a  bar chart of all the other student  submissions and because of the way that  learning tools interoperability works we  have to pass some information from the  we have to pass some information as we  go along through the process and when  you hit submit on a form it brings you  to a second page so that's one thing  that we cracked is making sure that we  pass all that information to the  following pages that  long so you can just use LTI launch form  so this is a second cloud object that  comes before and we just use LTI launch  form to make sure that the form is going  to pass all the data that needs to be  passed through okay so onto the real  projects that we were working on so this  launching innovations in schools course  is is on EDX a the teacher there asked  that we make an artefact generator they  wanted the students to at the beginning  of the course make a course plan so they  wanted them to reflect on when they  would work on the course what their  goals are stuff like that before the  course started so we made them this  artifact generator zoom in a little here  this artifact generator where they can  type in a bunch of information they can  pick their goals they can add another  goal they can say who they want to share  the course with they pick some time that  they would be working on the course and  add some goals and they can also add an  image and then they fill out the form  and it makes a nice little PDF for them  to then like maybe post near their desk  where they're going to work or something  like that and one of the great things  about how this works is now if i refresh  this page i can go back and get all of  the information that i had before  already saved in the forum and i can go  back and could submit and change the  information that I already had and we  did all of that without making them sign  into the Wolfram cloud because they've  already signed in to the course and we  can get that information through the  interoperability functionality so the  way that we do that is that there's a  function in a package that we've called  get user ID so basically I get the  hashed version of their authentication  to the course  and I can identify them within the  course using the user ID and I store  their information like all of the things  that they put int